<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-CSR half year net falls 24 percent.</title>
<headline>RTRS-CSR half year net falls 24 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30.</p>
<p>		     (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    238.6 vs  302.4</p>
<p>    Net				     154.7 vs  204.1</p>
<p>    Interim dividend (cents)	  12.0  vs   14.0</p>
<p>NOTE: CSR Ltd is a building products manufacturer and sugar and aluminium producer.  </p>
<p>    Sales  (bln)			 3.20 vs    3.14</p>
<p>    Other income (million)	     156.6  vs  164.1</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			 15.8  vs   20.4</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		     nil  vs gain 7.4</p>
<p>Dividend is 50 pct franked</p>
<p>Pay date Dec 18</p>
<p>Reg date Nov 29</p>
<p>    Tax				    76.0 vs  91.5</p>
<p>    Interest			     82.1 vs  75.4</p>
<p>    Depreciation			179.2 vs 165.5</p>
<p>    Minorities			    7.9 vs  14.2</p>
<p>NOTE:Divisional earnings after tax and minorities</p>
<p>    Construction materials	   23.9  vs  31.8</p>
<p>    Building materials		 18.8  vs  43.8</p>
<p>    Building materials-US	    78.5  vs  69.2</p>
<p>    Timber products		     0.3  vs  15.6</p>
<p>    Sugar				  54.1  vs  38.5</p>
<p>    Aluminium			    29.0  vs  40.5</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
